  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Born in Paris and raised in Cascais, Patrício Miguel Guerry Monteiro de Barros entered his family’s commercial affairs while still a student. He later joined Portuguese refiner Sonap and moved to the United States after nationalisation disrupted the business. At Philipp Brothers he built a career in international oil trading before becoming chief executive of Sigmoil and chairman of Argus Resources.\n\nBarros combined executive leadership with substantial energy investments. He held shares in Tosco before its sale to Phillips, served on Petrogal’s board and became chairman of European refiner Petroplus. His wider directorships included Portugal Telecom and Espírito Santo Financial Group. Outside business, he represented Portugal in Star-class sailing at the Seoul Olympics and remained a leading international competitor.",
    "html": "<p>Born in Paris and raised in Cascais, Patrício Miguel Guerry Monteiro de Barros entered his family’s commercial affairs while still a student. He later joined Portuguese refiner Sonap and moved to the United States after nationalisation disrupted the business. At Philipp Brothers he built a career in international oil trading before becoming chief executive of Sigmoil and chairman of Argus Resources.</p>\r\n<p>Barros combined executive leadership with substantial energy investments. He held shares in Tosco before its sale to Phillips, served on Petrogal’s board and became chairman of European refiner Petroplus. His wider directorships included Portugal Telecom and Espírito Santo Financial Group. Outside business, he represented Portugal in Star-class sailing at the Seoul Olympics and remained a leading international competitor.</p>\r\n",
